{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0167QzYbGCqMWuBCvdfBps52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# rnd-v10 â€” \"Live Handoff & Boneyard\" Build Session Summary\n\n- **All 8 waves completed GREEN; project DONE.** The build ran on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v10` (off master at v9 merge `9baabf0`), starting from baseline GREEN 1068 and ending at **GREEN 1189 passed, 1 skipped**. The branch is ready for John's merge + deploy decision â€” no merge to master / no `nssm restart anchor` until whole-branch sign-off.\n\n- **Wave 1 â€” paste-NOT-submit substrate (backend).** Added `paste_prompt=` to `terminal_session.start_session` (phase-1 seed still submitted; the task prompt held as `pending_paste`, written UNSENT once after the greet via `_flush_pending_paste`); new `session_registry` fields `pending_paste`/`paste_flushed`. Review caught a **BLOCKER premature flush** (greet marker was a substring of the echoed seed â†’ fired before any model greet) â€” fixed by counting marker occurrences *beyond* the seed's own base. Also fixed a double-paste TOCTOU (compare-and-set under `WRITE_LOCK`) and a missing newline strip. Ended GREEN 1083.\n\n- **Wave 2 â€” both-artifact advance + paste-in-panel (UI).** `handoff.build_next_stage_prompt` + `write_next_prompt` â†’ `NEXT-PROMPT.md`; advance/finish_to_build paths now deliver the prompt as a pending paste instead of an auto-submitted seed. Review flagged a non-discriminating Playwright token and a **North-Star hole** (`finish_to_build` marked planning DONE without persisting docs â†’ build checkout could lack referenced paths) â€” fixed by `capture_session_docs` (persist+commit, no reap) before advancing, plus a paste-only token assertion proven non-vacuous by sabotage. GREEN 1094; John signed off (453f687).\n\n- **Wave 3 â€” two toggleable grass terminals (UI).** Replaced the single shared grass terminal with two per-lane `.gterm` hosts (research + plan), each independently collapsible without killing the session. Review found a **BLOCKER ReferenceError** on grass Save (undeclared `panel`) masked by no test clicking Save â€” fixed by restoring `#grassPanel` lookup + making Save per-lane. Also hardened a flaky WS/SSE teardown race (`_is_benign_disconnect` returns cleanly on client disconnect). GREEN 1102; signed off (9594d89).\n\n- **Wave 4 â€” grass archive + grassâ†’project lineage.** New `effort_history.archive_grass_session` (persist dev docs + summary into a per-idea `archives` bundle, idea stays in grass); `session_registry.grass_origin` stamped/inherited through the chain. Review-driven fixes: inheritance now reaches the **chain root**, a board-tile \"from grass\" chip was implemented (fixing a `\"plan\"` vs `\"planning\"` column-key bug), dead-chip suppression, and idempotent archive. Added a systemic `conftest.py` flake-stabilization harness. GREEN 1123; signed off (bcbd3ca).\n\n- **Wave 5 â€” grass researchâ†’plan live handoff (UI).** `advance_grass_research_to_plan` persists research docs, builds the W2 prompt, and opens the contained `(idea,'plan')` dev session linked + paste-pending; honest-negative when no real research doc exists. Review found develop-plan-FIRST silently dropped the handoff and grass-dev sessions leaking onto the top strip â€” fixed via new `queue_paste` (deliver-on-focus, never double-paste) and top-strip containment filtering `[grass-dev]` labels. GREEN 1136; signed off (e506859).\n\n- **Wave 6 â€” Boneyard store + capture (backend, NEW `boneyard.py`).** Stdlib per-project index (`record_entry`/`list_entries`/`search`/`get_entry` + `build_session_entry`/`build_grass_entry`), index-not-copy referencing v8-persisted doc rels. Capture wired best-effort: killâ†’`killed`, delete_sessionâ†’`deleted` (before pointers drop, D10 ordering), delete_grass_ideaâ†’`grass-deleted`. Review found **two reproduced defects** masked by test blind spots: live-session delete recorded TWO entries (fixed via `kill(_record_boneyard=False)` â†’ exactly one `deleted`), and `build_grass_entry` omitted W4 archive-bundle docs (fixed by unioning archive docs). GREEN 1151 (bc0397e).\n\n- **Wave 7 â€” Boneyard UI.** `GET /api/rnd/boneyard?project_id=&q=` (token-gated, SAFE projection) + a \"â˜  Boneyard\" tab with search, source badges, and doc links routed through traversal-safe `/artifact`. Review caught a **HIGH stored-XSS** attribute breakout (client `_esc` didn't escape `\"`) and a timestamp tz divergence â€” fixed by hardening the shared `_esc` to full HTML-escape (verified all 24 callers safe) and unifying both render paths on a server-computed `when_display`. GREEN 1163; signed off (6c1c2ab).\n\n- **Wave 8 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck + distro + docs (PROJECT DONE).** Added read-only `anchor.py` mirrors `rnd boneyard` and `rnd next-prompt` (never starts a session/model), plus fully-stubbed `check_rnd_v10_surface`. GATE 1 caught that the test count hadn't grown (missing per-version regression files) â†’ added `test_cli_v10.py` (20) + `test_healthcheck_v10.py` (6). Review fixed two **doc-overclaims** in CLAUDE.md (Boneyard links route through `/artifact` for ALL sources; researchâ†’plan writes only `NEXT-PROMPT.md`, HANDOFF.md conditional on a discoverable plan set). Final GREEN 1189.\n\n- **Process note: adversarial review consistently surfaced real, test-masked defects.** Across waves the 2-independent-reviewer refute loop caught blockers/highs (premature flush, Save ReferenceError, stored-XSS, double-Boneyard-entry) that the passing test suite had missed, and every fix was proven non-vacuous against the pre-fix code. Test-flake determinism was a recurring theme (WS/SSE teardown races, a greet-injectâ†’flush render race) addressed at both product and fixture level."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8548,"cache_read_input_tokens":80459,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h